\f0\b\fs32 \cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What changed, and on which token\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa195\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 An RPE row cannot exist before its session ends
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0The row is built from the session's end time against the club-local clock, so a session still to come produces nothing. In the Full frame the 16:00 team run is 40 minutes away and has no row; the only RPE row is the 10:00 gym session, which finished at 11:15. The state called out in the brief is now unrepresentable in this board.\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 no token change \'97 a data rule. Subtitle stays --font-num / --t-body-xs / --muted with tabular-nums
\f1\fs26 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 RPE rows say when the session was
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0The subtitle carries the session time ahead of the duration: "Today 11:15 \'b7 20 sec" for one earlier today, "Yesterday \'b7 20 sec" for one carried over, "\{Day\} HH:MM \'b7 20 sec" for anything older. Tabular figures keep the times aligned down a stack of rows.\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 --font-num + font-variant-numeric tabular-nums \'b7 --t-body-xs / --w-regular / --muted
\f1\fs26 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Multiple RPE rows run oldest first
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0Two outstanding tasks are ordered by session end time, so yesterday's gym session sits above this morning's team run. The oldest is the one most at risk of being forgotten and the one whose recall is worst, so it is the one the thumb reaches first.\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 ordering only \'b7 rows unchanged at --surf / 1px --border / --r / --shadow
\f1\fs26 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Availability uses the tone-family card, not a stripe
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0Modified and Unavailable now take fill, border and foreground from one tone family \'97 the documented card-level urgency device. Nothing is alpha-muted on the tint: body copy sits at the family's own foreground rather than --muted, and the status pill inverts to a white chip so it still reads as a chip on a tinted ground.\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 modified --pill-warn + 1px --warn + --on-warn \'b7 unavailable --pill-bad + 1px --bad + --on-bad \'b7 pill --surf chip + --on-warn / --on-bad \'b7 divider rgba(var(--warn-rgb), 0.45)
\f1\fs26 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Modified and Unavailable also surface above To do
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0A single-line Banner sits between the greeting and To do carrying the status and a short reason, linking down to the full card, which keeps all of its content. Full shows no banner: an all-clear does not need to interrupt, and the card below still states it.\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 Banner tone warn / bad \'b7 --r-round dot \'b7 message --text
\f1\fs26 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 No glyph tiles
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0WEL, RPE and NUT are gone. Each row is title, timed subtitle and chevron, which lets a row sit at the 44px minimum instead of the 82px the 44px tiles forced, and the titles carry the domain on their own.\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 row padding 16px 18px, min-height 44px \'b7 --r \'b7 --shadow \'b7 chevron --t-card-lg / --faint
\f1\fs26 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Diagnosis and team render whenever their data exists
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0The medical block sits inside the availability card under a "visible to you and medical staff" eyebrow \'97 the athlete is one of the two parties permitted to see it. "Team this week" renders below the card whenever a team is set. Both appear in Modified and Unavailable and are absent from the three Available frames, where neither has data.\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 eyebrow --t-eyebrow + --t-eyebrow-tracking at the tone foreground \'b7 body --t-body-xs
\f1\fs26 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 The list is its own status
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0The count reads "3 left" or "None left" off the same array the rows render from, so it cannot disagree with them, and with nothing outstanding the To do slot holds one row-shaped card reading "You're up to date" rather than an empty region. The greeting is club-local \'97 every frame here is one instant, Thu 10 Sept 15:20 Europe/London, which is what makes "Afternoon" and every session time consistent.\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 count in the Eyebrow primitive \'b7 empty card --surf / --border / --r / --shadow, same geometry as a row
\f1\fs26 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Needs new token\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Nothing
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 \'a0No new colour, radius, spacing step, type size or duration. Two items that were exceptions in earlier passes are now closed rather than carried: the off-scale 1.0625rem row name is on --t-num-row, and the stripe-on-a-card is replaced by the documented tone-family treatment. The one open item is not a token but the code question above.\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 --t-num-row 17px \'b7 --pill-warn / --on-warn \'b7 --pill-bad / --on-bad
\f1\fs26 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

